* ====================================================================
* IBM MQ 9.4 - Auckland Gateway / Full Repository Queue Manager (QM_AKL_FR)
* ====================================================================

* 1. Close Channel Authentication and Connection Authentication
ALTER QMGR CONNAUTH('') CHLAUTH(DISABLED)
REFRESH SECURITY
ALTER QMGR CCSID(1208)

* 2. appoint DEADQ
DEFINE QLOCAL(DEADQ) REPLACE
ALTER QMGR DEADQ(DEADQ)

* 3. Define Cluster and alter QMGR to act as Full Repository
ALTER QMGR REPOS(AKL_CLUSTER)

* Define Cluster Receiver Channel (Full Repository)
DEFINE CHANNEL(TO.QM_AKL_FR) CHLTYPE(CLUSRCVR) TRPTYPE(TCP) +
  CONNAME('mq-akl-fr(1414)') CLUSTER(AKL_CLUSTER) +
  DESCR('Cluster Receiver channel for QM_AKL_FR') REPLACE

* 4. Define Gateway Queue Alias (网关别名队列)
* Clients (like Spring Boot) send payments to 'PAYMENT.TX.INBOUND'.
* This queue manager acts as a gateway and doesn't host the actual physical queue.
* Instead, it defines an Alias pointing to the clustered target queue 'PAYMENT.CLUSTER.IN'.
* DEFBIND(NOTFIXED) ensures that workload balancing (round-robin) happens on a per-message basis.
DEFINE QALIAS(PAYMENT.TX.INBOUND) TARGET(PAYMENT.CLUSTER.IN) +
  DEFBIND(NOTFIXED) DESCR('Gateway Queue Alias for Clustered Payment Queue') REPLACE

DEFINE CHANNEL('DEV.ADMIN.SVRCONN') CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) TRPTYPE(TCP) MCAUSER('mqm') REPLACE
DEFINE QREMOTE(QM_ALK) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL(PAYMENT.CROSSBORDER.OUT) CLUSTER(AKL_CLUSTER) DEFPSIST(YES) REPLACE